{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Spell of the Unpleasant: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja61'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 61 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>1. Asātamantajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Spell of the Unpleasant: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Asā lokitthiyo nāma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The women in the world called unclaimed—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>velā tāsaṁ na vijjati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>there is no confining them. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sārattā ca pagabbhā ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>They are rude and full of desires, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sikhī sabbaghaso yathā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like an all-consuming flame. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tā hitvā pabbajissāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Leaving them behind, I shall go forth </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vivekamanubrūhayan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and foster seclusion. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Asātamantajātakaṁ paṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
